  "contract": "Linux filenames are byte strings, so two names that differ only in invalid UTF-8 bytes name two distinct directory entries.",
  "observed": "Source reading predicts that f\\x80 and f\\x81 both resolve to \"f\\u{FFFD}\", so the second O_EXCL create collides with the first. This has not run on Asterinas.",
